2026-09-27T07:55:07.2283737Z Update Note
2026-09-27T07:55:07.2284050Z ===========
2026-09-27T07:55:07.2284504Z Please use this repository instead of ppa:fkrull/deadsnakes.
2026-09-27T07:55:07.2284888Z 
2026-09-27T07:55:07.2284980Z Reporting Issues
2026-09-27T07:55:07.2285187Z ================
2026-09-27T07:55:07.2285299Z 
2026-09-27T07:55:07.2285453Z Issues can be reported in the master issue tracker at:
2026-09-27T07:55:07.2285811Z https://github.com/deadsnakes/issues/issues
2026-09-27T07:55:07.2286024Z 
2026-09-27T07:55:07.2286139Z Supported Ubuntu and Python Versions
2026-09-27T07:55:07.2286416Z ====================================
2026-09-27T07:55:07.2286588Z 
2026-09-27T07:55:07.2286723Z - Ubuntu 22.04 (jammy) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.10)
2026-09-27T07:55:07.2287425Z - Ubuntu 24.04 (noble) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.12)
2026-09-27T07:55:07.2289248Z - Ubuntu 26.04 (resolute) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.14)
2026-09-27T07:55:07.2290418Z - Note: Python 3.10 (jammy), Python3.12 (noble), Python3.14 (resolute) are not provided by deadsnakes as upstream ubuntu provides those packages.
2026-09-27T07:55:07.2291295Z 
2026-09-27T07:55:07.2291469Z Why some packages aren't built:
2026-09-27T07:55:07.2292152Z - Note: for 22.04+, older python versions requre libssl<3 so they are not currently built
2026-09-27T07:55:07.2293079Z - If you need these, reach out to asottile to set up a private ppa
2026-09-27T07:55:07.2293532Z 
2026-09-27T07:55:07.2294017Z The packages may also work on other versions of Ubuntu or Debian, but that is not tested or supported.
2026-09-27T07:55:07.2294742Z 
2026-09-27T07:55:07.2294889Z Packages
2026-09-27T07:55:07.2295113Z ========
2026-09-27T07:55:07.2295219Z 
2026-09-27T07:55:07.2296455Z The packages provided here are loosely based on the debian upstream packages with some modifications to make them more usable as non-default pythons and on ubuntu.  As such, the packages follow debian's patterns and often do not include a full python distribution with just `apt install python#.#`.  Here is a list of packages that may be useful along with the default install:
2026-09-27T07:55:07.2298013Z 
2026-09-27T07:55:07.2298233Z - `python#.#-dev`: includes development headers for building C extensions
2026-09-27T07:55:07.2298698Z - `python#.#-venv`: provides the standard library `venv` module
2026-09-27T07:55:07.2299557Z - `python#.#-distutils`: provides the standard library `distutils` module
2026-09-27T07:55:07.2366098Z - `python#.#-lib2to3`: provides the `2to3-#.#` utility as well as the standard library `lib2to3` module
2026-09-27T07:55:07.2367428Z - `python#.#-gdbm`: provides the standard library `dbm.gnu` module
2026-09-27T07:55:07.2368361Z - `python#.#-tk`: provides the standard library `tkinter` module
2026-09-27T07:55:07.2369316Z 
2026-09-27T07:55:07.2369482Z Third-Party Python Modules
2026-09-27T07:55:07.2369866Z ==========================
2026-09-27T07:55:07.2370104Z 
2026-09-27T07:55:07.2371810Z Python modules in the official Ubuntu repositories are packaged to work with the Python interpreters from the official repositories. Accordingly, they generally won't work with the Python interpreters from this PPA. As an exception, pure-Python modules for Python 3 will work, but any compiled extension modules won't.
2026-09-27T07:55:07.2373767Z 
2026-09-27T07:55:07.2374853Z To install 3rd-party Python modules, you should use the common Python packaging tools.  For an introduction into the Python packaging ecosystem and its tools, refer to the Python Packaging User Guide:
2026-09-27T07:55:07.2376367Z https://packaging.python.org/installing/
2026-09-27T07:55:07.2376752Z 
